  "name": "guile-goblins",
  "description": "A distributed object programming environment ported to GNU Guile, implementing a transactional actor model rooted in Object Capability (OCap) security principles. It facilitates secure, distributed asynchronous message passing across heterogeneous netlayers—including Tor/Onion and libp2p—using the CapTP and OCapN protocols. The system features integrated persistence, a dedicated serialization format known as Syrup, and cross-platform capabilities via WebAssembly integration.",
